哦，观察得真仔细。

1418
01:01:13.650 --> 01:01:20.950
Yeah, but Dwight gets this phone call from a client saying that Michael Scott Paper Company
对，但德怀特接到了一个客户的电话，说迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司

1419
01:01:20.950 --> 01:01:25.230
called them and asked them for more money, and they'd like to come back to Dunder Mifflin.
打电话向他们索要更多钱，他们想回到邓德米夫林。

1420
01:01:25.510 --> 01:01:28.170
And Dwight's going to run into the kitchen and tattle.
然后德怀特跑进厨房去告状。

1421
01:01:28.350 --> 01:01:31.030
He's going to tell Charles, Michael Scott Paper Company is going broke.
他要告诉查尔斯，迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司快破产了。

1422
01:01:31.190 --> 01:01:36.170
And normally, Charles would take that information from Dwight and go right into action.
按常理，查尔斯听到德怀特提供的情报后会立刻采取行动。

1423
01:01:36.390 --> 01:01:39.110
But Dwight's been acting so strange to Charles all day.
但德怀特一整天对查尔斯表现得太奇怪了。

1424
01:01:39.110 --> 01:01:41.710
And then Jim capitalizes on that.
然后吉姆就利用了这一点。

1425
01:01:42.130 --> 01:01:50.330
Yeah, he kind of baits Dwight into bringing out his full weirdo by sort of heckling him
对，他有点像是在通过嘲讽德怀特

1426
01:01:50.330 --> 01:01:52.530
about his ability to solve cases.
破案的能力，来引出德怀特怪咖的本质。

1427
01:01:52.670 --> 01:01:54.490
And Charles is like, you're both morons.
而查尔斯的反应是，你们两个都是笨蛋。

1428
01:01:54.490 --> 01:01:56.630
Don't go anywhere near the conference room.
离会议室远点。

1429
01:01:56.830 --> 01:02:00.250
Here's what I need to bring up about this scene on a practical level.
关于这个场景，我需要从实际操作层面提一点。

1430
01:02:00.370 --> 01:02:03.190
Did you notice where Charles is standing in this scene?
你们注意到查尔斯在这个场景里站在哪里吗？

1431
01:02:03.350 --> 01:02:04.270
By the counter?
在柜台旁边？

1432
01:02:04.610 --> 01:02:06.770
Yes, but very close to the fridge.
是的，而且离冰箱非常近。

1433
01:02:06.770 --> 01:02:11.470
And through the entire scene, he's got his Sadekoy steel coffee mug.
在整场戏中，他一直拿着他的萨德科伊钢制咖啡杯。

1434
01:02:11.610 --> 01:02:11.930
Yeah.
对。

1435
01:02:12.090 --> 01:02:14.370
And he's got a full coffee pot.
而且他手里还拿着满满一壶咖啡。

1436
01:02:14.550 --> 01:02:16.570
Each hand is holding one of these iteMs.
他两只手各拿一样东西。

1437
01:02:17.130 --> 01:02:24.090
Why did he walk so far away from the coffee maker to put his coffee in his mug?
他为什么拿着咖啡杯走到离咖啡机那么远的地方？

1438
01:02:24.250 --> 01:02:27.670
Because the coffee maker is over by the door that leads to the office.
因为咖啡机在通往办公室的门旁边。

1439
01:02:27.990 --> 01:02:32.270
So this man is saddled with these two coffee iteMs.
所以这个人身上挂着这两样与咖啡相关的物件。

1440
01:02:32.410 --> 01:02:34.310
And I'm just like, why did he drift?
我就想，他为什么要走开呢？

1441
01:02:34.310 --> 01:02:39.550
In my mind as an actor, I'm having to make up a reason why this happened.
作为一名演员，我脑子里不得不为发生这种事编造一个理由。

1442
01:02:39.710 --> 01:02:45.110
So I'm imagining he got the coffee pot and he's starting to pour and he notices something
所以我脑补的是他拿了咖啡壶正要倒咖啡，然后他注意到了

1443
01:02:45.110 --> 01:02:45.750
on the fridge.
冰箱上的某个东西。

1444
01:02:45.890 --> 01:02:47.410
He wants to get a closer look.
他想仔细看一看。

1445
01:02:47.710 --> 01:02:52.510
And then Dwight comes in and he's now stuck with his two coffees.
接着德怀特进来了，然后他就被这两杯咖啡给绊住了。

1446
01:02:52.770 --> 01:02:53.550
I don't know.
我不知道。

1447
01:02:53.710 --> 01:02:55.470
It was an odd staging for me.
对我来说这个舞台调度很奇怪。

1448
01:02:55.610 --> 01:02:56.830
And I became distracted.
然后我就分心了。

1449
01:02:57.190 --> 01:02:59.870
I love that like this moment pulled you out for a minute.
我喜欢这种让你瞬间出戏的时刻。

1450
01:03:00.070 --> 01:03:02.770
Like as an actor process, you're like, that makes no sense.
就演员的创作过程而言，你会觉得这完全讲不通。

1451
01:03:02.770 --> 01:03:04.110
I'm like, I need a reason.
我觉得吧，我得有个理由。

1452
01:03:04.410 --> 01:03:05.690
I need a motivation.
我需要一个动力。

1453
01:03:06.130 --> 01:03:11.550
Back in the conference room, Michael says no to this very lucrative offer.
回到会议室里，迈克尔拒绝了这份非常丰厚的报价。

1454
01:03:11.810 --> 01:03:12.090
Yeah.
没错。

1455
01:03:12.210 --> 01:03:14.090
And Pam is like, can we have another minute?
而帕姆就说，能再给我们一分钟吗？

1456
01:03:14.370 --> 01:03:14.670
Yeah.
对。

1457
01:03:14.930 --> 01:03:18.350
And this is when Michael again makes perfect sense.
而这时，迈克尔再次表现得极为通情达理。

1458
01:03:18.350 --> 01:03:21.230
And he says, what we need are jobs.
他说，我们需要的是工作。

1459
01:03:21.490 --> 01:03:22.930
We don't need a buyout.
我们不需要买断费。

1460
01:03:23.150 --> 01:03:24.510
That money's not going to last forever.
这笔钱是不可能花一辈子的。

1461
01:03:24.670 --> 01:03:25.470
We need employment.
我们需要就业。

1462
01:03:25.470 --> 01:03:26.710
And everyone agrees.
大家都表示赞同。

1463
01:03:27.030 --> 01:03:27.250
Yes.
是的。

1464
01:03:27.370 --> 01:03:29.250
This is his teach a man to fish moment.
这就是他那次“授人以鱼不如授人以渔”的高光时刻。

1465
01:03:29.450 --> 01:03:29.890
Yes.
没错。

1466
01:03:30.030 --> 01:03:30.230
Right?
对吧？

1467
01:03:30.230 --> 01:03:33.930
So when they come back in, that's what Michael is going to say.
所以当他们再次走进去时，迈克尔就会这么说。

1468
01:03:34.030 --> 01:03:35.970
You have to hire all of us back.
你们必须把我们所有人重新雇佣。

1469
01:03:36.170 --> 01:03:40.050
And also, in addition to jobs, Michael wants his Sebring again.
而且，除了工作之外，迈克尔还想要回他的赛百灵（Sebring）。

1470
01:03:40.270 --> 01:03:41.570
And his old parking space.
还有他原来的停车位。

1471
01:03:41.930 --> 01:03:45.370
But Charles says they don't make Sebrings anymore.
但查尔斯说他们不再生产赛百灵了。

1472
01:03:45.910 --> 01:03:46.910
Is that true?
那是真的吗？

1473
01:03:47.370 --> 01:03:49.290
Lady, you know I had to know.
女士，你知道我必须去查清楚。

1474
01:03:49.470 --> 01:03:53.750
Oh, I'm so glad you looked this up because I didn't look it up and it has been bothering me.
哦，我太高兴你查了这事，因为我没查，这事一直困扰着我。

1475
01:03:53.870 --> 01:03:54.310
All right.
好了。

1476
01:03:54.670 --> 01:03:55.770
Charles is wrong.
查尔斯错了。

1477
01:03:55.770 --> 01:03:58.130
They are still making the Sebring.
他们还在生产赛百灵。

1478
01:03:58.310 --> 01:04:01.270
This episode aired April of 2009.
这集播出于2009年4月。

1479
01:04:01.690 --> 01:04:08.410
According to the internet, they made the Chrysler Sebring from 1995 to 2010.
根据网上的资料，克莱斯勒赛百灵从1995年一直生产到2010年。

1480
01:04:08.950 --> 01:04:14.710
And in looking up this fact, I ended up watching several Sebring commercials over the years.
为了核实这个事实，我最后看了好几个历年的赛百灵广告。

1481
01:04:14.930 --> 01:04:15.490
Oh.
哦。

1482
01:04:16.050 --> 01:04:18.750
You really were infested.
你真的是中毒太深了。

1483
01:04:18.750 --> 01:04:22.110
I think I watched half an hour worth of commercials.
我想我看了足足半小时的广告。

1484
01:04:23.730 --> 01:04:24.670
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1485
01:04:24.830 --> 01:04:27.430
They made some really interesting choices in their commercials.
他们在广告里做了一些非常有趣的尝试。

1486
01:04:27.790 --> 01:04:29.990
But there's one I really needed you to hear.
但有一个广告我是真觉得必须得让你们听听。

1487
01:04:30.370 --> 01:04:31.790
It is from 1995.
那是1995年的。

1488
01:04:32.170 --> 01:04:34.030
It's the year the car debuted.
正是这款车问世的那一年。

1489
01:04:34.390 --> 01:04:36.830
Can we please play that Sebring commercial?
我们能播一下那个赛百灵广告吗？

1490
01:04:37.550 --> 01:04:42.410
The new Chrysler Sebring was built upon something called the Goldilocks principle.
全新克莱斯勒赛百灵是基于所谓的“金发姑娘原则”打造的。

1491
01:04:42.790 --> 01:04:47.650
It occurred to us that while most luxury cars were too big, most sport coupes were too small.
我们发现，当大多数豪华车显得过大时，大多数跑车又显得太小。

1492
01:04:47.970 --> 01:04:51.650
We wanted the Sebring to be, well, just right.
我们希望赛百灵能做到——嗯，恰到好处。

1493
01:04:51.930 --> 01:04:56.690
It not only has a sporty 24-valve engine and a race-inspired suspension,
它不仅配备了动感的24气门发动机和赛车级悬挂，

1494
01:04:57.210 --> 01:05:00.250
but it also gives you the luxury of an actual backseat.
还为你提供了真正后排座椅的奢华享受。

1495
01:05:00.430 --> 01:05:02.770
Which means there's enough room for Goldilocks.
这意味着有足够金发姑娘坐的空间。

1496
01:05:03.010 --> 01:05:05.250
And three or four of our friends.
以及我们的三四个朋友。

1497
01:05:07.650 --> 01:05:12.100
I have to say, okay, so Sam is not with us this week.
我得说，好吧，萨姆这周没有和我们在一起。

1498
01:05:12.240 --> 01:05:12.840
He's on vacation.
他在度假。

1499
01:05:13.060 --> 01:05:14.140
Jordan is filling in.
乔丹来代班。

1500
01:05:14.260 --> 01:05:16.000
And it is like laughing.
而且简直笑死人了。

1501
01:05:16.220 --> 01:05:19.500
I can see her laughing at that commercial.
我能看到她在看那个广告时笑呢。

1502
01:05:20.120 --> 01:05:20.760
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们，伙计们。

1503
01:05:21.180 --> 01:05:24.600
When watching my half an hour of Chrysler commercials for the Sebring,
当我看了半小时克莱斯勒赛百灵的广告后，

1504
01:05:24.740 --> 01:05:25.960
I'd had a glass of wine.
我当时喝了一杯酒。

1505
01:05:26.440 --> 01:05:29.860
And when we got to this one, I literally did a spit take.
而当我们看到这个广告时，我真的把水喷出来了。

1506
01:05:30.020 --> 01:05:30.840
I was like, what?
我当时就想，什么鬼？

1507
01:05:31.540 --> 01:05:34.120
And the whole time the car is driving through the woods.
而且整个过程中这辆车都在树林里开着。

1508
01:05:34.640 --> 01:05:35.040
Okay.
好吧。

1509
01:05:35.380 --> 01:05:36.500
Oh, because of Goldilocks.
哦，因为金发姑娘。

1510
01:05:36.560 --> 01:05:37.480
And the three bears.
还有三只熊。

1511
01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:37.800
Yeah.
对。

1512
01:05:37.800 --> 01:05:40.640
But when they were like, to fit a few of her friends.
但当他们说什么“能坐下她的几个朋友”时。

1513
01:05:44.390 --> 01:05:45.430
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

1514
01:05:45.450 --> 01:05:46.250
I had to share that.
我不得不分享一下那个。

1515
01:05:46.430 --> 01:05:48.270
So, yes, they still had the Sebring.
所以，是的，他们当时确实还在生产赛百灵。

1516
01:05:48.390 --> 01:05:51.550
They could have given Michael a Sebring in April of 2009.
他们本可以在2009年4月给迈克一辆赛百灵的。

1517
01:05:52.110 --> 01:05:58.150
By the way, I want to say, you know my friend Stacy, who I invented the tan baster with?
顺便说一句，我想说，你知道我那个和我一起发明防晒喷枪的朋友斯黛西吗？

1518
01:05:58.390 --> 01:05:58.810
Yes.
知道。

1519
01:05:58.990 --> 01:06:00.130
She drove a Sebring.
她就开一辆赛百灵。

1520
01:06:00.370 --> 01:06:00.770
Oh.
哦。

1521
01:06:00.770 --> 01:06:02.350
And it was a lovely car.
而且那是一辆很棒的车。

1522
01:06:02.350 --> 01:06:06.030
I have to say, it was kind of like, they're right.
我得说，感觉就像是，他们说得对。

1523
01:06:06.210 --> 01:06:11.410
It was a really nice combination of a sporty coupe, but also roomy.
它确实完美结合了跑车的动感与宽敞的空间。

1524
01:06:11.530 --> 01:06:12.830
But with a comfortable backseat.
而且后排座位很舒服。

1525
01:06:13.070 --> 01:06:13.690
I don't know.
我不知道。

1526
01:06:13.750 --> 01:06:14.850
I never sat in the backseat.
我从没坐过后排。

1527
01:06:15.010 --> 01:06:16.830
Well, Goldilocks would have been happy with it.
好吧，金发姑娘肯定会对它满意的。

1528
01:06:16.830 --> 01:06:18.010
She could have sat back there.
她完全可以坐在后面。

1529
01:06:18.770 --> 01:06:24.670
Also, since we brought up Jordan, Jordan did our song parody, Total Eclipse of the Fart.
另外，既然我们提到了乔丹，乔丹给我们创作了恶搞歌曲《放屁的日全食》。

1530
01:06:24.950 --> 01:06:25.290
Yes.
是的。

1531
01:06:25.390 --> 01:06:26.830
That was Jordan who sang that.
那是乔丹唱的。

1532
01:06:27.030 --> 01:06:28.170
We're very happy to have you.
我们非常高兴你能来。

1533
01:06:28.270 --> 01:06:29.790
Thank you for filling in for Sam today.
谢谢你今天代替萨姆。

1534
01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:30.250
Yes.
是的。

1535
01:06:30.310 --> 01:06:31.750
Sam, I brought cake today.
萨姆，我今天带了蛋糕。

1536
01:06:31.750 --> 01:06:33.150
So, you missed out on that.
所以，你错过了。

1537
01:06:33.150 --> 01:06:35.610
I also got it on my sweater as I walked in.
我刚才走进来的时候，它还蹭到我的毛衣上了。

1538
01:06:35.850 --> 01:06:36.170
Yeah.
对。

1539
01:06:36.330 --> 01:06:38.350
I noticed it right away when you walked in.
你一进来我就注意到了。

1540
01:06:38.490 --> 01:06:41.250
And I thought, I don't know, it's ketchup or something.
我还心想，不知道是什么，番茄酱还是什么的。

1541
01:06:41.450 --> 01:06:43.190
You thought I had a messy breakfaSt.
你以为我吃早饭弄得很脏。

1542
01:06:43.490 --> 01:06:44.230
I guess I did.
我想我确实是。

1543
01:06:44.230 --> 01:06:44.990
I guess I did.
我想我确实是。

1544
01:06:45.130 --> 01:06:48.230
I thought it was left over maybe from the last time you wore it.
我还以为可能是上次穿的时候留下的呢。

1545
01:06:48.290 --> 01:06:48.770
Jenna.
珍娜。

1546
01:06:49.170 --> 01:06:49.450
What?
什么？

1547
01:06:50.010 --> 01:06:54.590
I wouldn't leave food on my hoodie and hang it back up.
我才不会把食物留在卫衣上然后又挂回去呢。

1548
01:06:54.730 --> 01:06:56.710
If you didn't notice, you might.
如果你没注意到，说不定还真会。

1549
01:06:56.910 --> 01:06:58.990
Have you never not noticed?
你从来没有没注意到的时候吗？

1550
01:06:59.870 --> 01:07:02.030
It's a pretty big mark right on my boob.
这就在我胸口上，是个挺大的印记呢。

1551
01:07:02.030 --> 01:07:05.030
I love that my husband, though, didn't say a word as I walked out.
不过我挺喜欢我丈夫的，我走出去时他一句话也没说。

1552
01:07:05.190 --> 01:07:06.210
Josh, come on.
乔希，快点。

1553
01:07:06.730 --> 01:07:07.390
All right.
好啦。

1554
01:07:07.590 --> 01:07:09.270
So, back to this episode.
那么，回到这一集。

1555
01:07:09.450 --> 01:07:12.270
Would you like to hear how the expense report finished?
你们想听听费用报销单是怎么结尾的吗？

1556
01:07:12.450 --> 01:07:12.990
Yes, please.
想听，请讲。

1557
01:07:13.250 --> 01:07:20.930
Because in the script, this is where it would have wrapped up Angela and Andy, their final scene about the expense report.
因为在剧本里，安吉拉和安迪关于费用报销单的最后一幕本来应该在这里结束。

1558
01:07:21.870 --> 01:07:27.630
And now, with no further red-ed-ed-ed-a-do, my revised expense report.
现在，废话不多说，这是我修改后的费用报销单。

1559
01:07:27.630 --> 01:07:28.030
The deadline's passed.
截止日期已经过了。

1560
01:07:28.030 --> 01:07:28.230
What?
什么？

1561
01:07:28.650 --> 01:07:29.010
When?
什么时候？

1562
01:07:29.270 --> 01:07:30.790
When you were saying red-ed-ed-ed-do.
就在你说“废话不多说”的时候。

1563
01:07:32.410 --> 01:07:34.310
It's red-ed-ed-a-do.
是“废话不多说”没错。

1564
01:07:34.490 --> 01:07:34.790
I know.
我知道。

1565
01:07:34.870 --> 01:07:36.010
I've always been such a fan of it.
我一直很喜欢这个。

1566
01:07:40.320 --> 01:07:41.400
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1567
01:07:42.280 --> 01:07:43.880
Isn't that so delicious?
是不是很妙？

1568
01:07:44.580 --> 01:07:46.080
I'm really sad that got cut.
这段被剪掉我真的觉得好难过。

1569
01:07:46.560 --> 01:07:47.500
Me, too.
我也是。

1570
01:07:47.860 --> 01:07:54.040
Oh, and as soon as he was like, I just turn around and I don't look at him anymore and he has to walk away.
哦，而且他一那样，我就转过身去再也不看他，然后他只好走开。

1571
01:07:54.040 --> 01:07:56.320
Well, I have some news for Angela.
好吧，我有个消息要告诉安吉拉。

1572
01:07:57.040 --> 01:08:05.140
This power that she's had is going to go away because Michael, Pam, and Ryan get their jobs back.
她拥有的这种权力要消失了，因为迈克尔、帕姆和瑞恩官复原职了。

1573
01:08:05.520 --> 01:08:05.920
Yep.
没错。

1574
01:08:06.160 --> 01:08:07.340
That's the buyout.
这就是收购协议。

1575
01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:10.700
The buyout is that they are all now re-employed by Dunder Mifflin.
收购协议的内容是他们现在都被邓德米弗林重新雇用了。

1576
01:08:10.700 --> 01:08:14.720
And I guess, is Charles fired?
我想问，查尔斯被解雇了吗？

1577
01:08:14.780 --> 01:08:16.580
That was never clear to me.
这一点我一直不太清楚。

1578
01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:18.000
No, I don't think he was fired.
不，我觉得他没被解雇。

1579
01:08:18.080 --> 01:08:20.400
He's going to show up in Company Picnic again.
他会在《公司野餐》里再次出现。

1580
01:08:20.600 --> 01:08:21.100
Yeah, no.
对，没错。

1581
01:08:21.240 --> 01:08:27.580
My understanding, and I re-read the script, so sort of what I inferred is that he's just getting reassigned.
我的理解是，而且我重读了剧本，我推测的情况是，他只是被调职了。

1582
01:08:27.800 --> 01:08:30.500
Well, he's going to be out of Scranton, obviously.
嗯，显然他要离开斯克兰顿了。

1583
01:08:31.060 --> 01:08:33.820
But originally, Michael says, I want him fired.
但原本迈克尔说：“我想让他被开除。”

1584
01:08:33.820 --> 01:08:35.620
And David's like, I'm not going to do that, Michael.
然后大卫说：“我不会那样做的，迈克尔。”

1585
01:08:35.880 --> 01:08:36.100
Yeah.
对。

1586
01:08:36.420 --> 01:08:37.600
No, he's a good employee.
不，他是个好员工。

1587
01:08:37.900 --> 01:08:42.620
He's maybe not a good fit right here in the Scranton branch, but he's going to still have his other branches.
他可能不太适合斯克兰顿分公司，但他仍然管辖着他的其他分公司。

1588
01:08:42.880 --> 01:08:43.740
To manage.
去管理。

1589
01:08:43.920 --> 01:08:44.300
To manage.
去管理。

1590
01:08:44.580 --> 01:08:44.860
To oversee.
去监督。

1591
01:08:45.140 --> 01:08:45.380
That's right.
没错。

1592
01:08:45.500 --> 01:08:46.280
That's how I saw it.
我是这么看的。

1593
01:08:46.420 --> 01:08:46.700
Okay.
好的。

1594
01:08:47.080 --> 01:08:54.600
Because the whole thing kind of ends with Charles trying to say goodbye, but Michael says, no, no, you're done.
因为整件事的结尾是查尔斯试图道别，但迈克尔说：“不，不，你不用说了。”

1595
01:08:55.140 --> 01:08:59.420
And that's the same line that Charles said to Michael in two weeks.
这跟两周前查尔斯对迈克尔说的话是一样的。

1596
01:08:59.620 --> 01:09:00.000
Oh.
哦。

1597
01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:01.720
So this is some good Michael sass.
所以这是迈克尔精彩的毒舌回击。

1598
01:09:01.940 --> 01:09:03.280
Yeah, Michael held on to that.
对，迈克尔一直把这句话记在心里。

1599
01:09:03.420 --> 01:09:04.120
He really did.
他真的记着呢。

1600
01:09:04.460 --> 01:09:13.320
And then there's this talking head by Michael that kind of ends the episode where he's just sort of wrapping up this whole storyline of having had this paper company.
然后是迈克尔的一段独白，算是给这一整条拥有这家造纸公司的故事线画上了句号。

1601
01:09:13.580 --> 01:09:16.040
And Randy shared with us that this was added later.
兰迪和我们分享说，这一段是后来加的。

1602
01:09:16.140 --> 01:09:17.540
It was not in the original script.
它并不在最初的剧本里。

1603
01:09:17.660 --> 01:09:21.380
They even shot it about two weeks after we shot the rest of this episode.
他们甚至在我们拍完这集其余部分大约两周后才补拍了这幕。

1604
01:09:21.620 --> 01:09:24.540
Do you want to know what was in the original shooting draft?
你们想知道最初的拍摄定稿里有什么吗？

1605
01:09:24.700 --> 01:09:25.520
Yes, please.
想啊，请告诉我们。

1606
01:09:26.080 --> 01:09:30.040
Well, there were two final goodbyes to Charles that got cut.
嗯，原本有两个对查尔斯最后的道别被删掉了。

1607
01:09:30.320 --> 01:09:33.680
Any guesses who would want to make sure they said goodbye to Charles, Jenna?
珍娜，你猜谁会想要确保自己向查尔斯道别？

1608
01:09:33.680 --> 01:09:40.220
Um, I'm imagining it was the ladies who had their ear to the door who fought over a scarf in the rain.
嗯，我猜是那两个在门边偷听、还在雨中为一条围巾争抢的女士。

1609
01:09:40.220 --> 01:09:42.240
Yes, Angela and Kelly.
没错，安吉拉和凯莉。

1610
01:09:42.760 --> 01:09:44.980
So in the script, there was this tag.
所以在剧本里，有这么个尾声片段。

1611
01:09:44.980 --> 01:09:49.160
As Charles is leaving, Angela approaches him and she says,
在查尔斯离开时，安吉拉走近他说道，

1612
01:09:49.160 --> 01:09:50.620
It was an honor.
这是我的荣幸。

1613
01:09:50.800 --> 01:09:51.940
And Charles says,
查尔斯则说，

1614
01:09:52.360 --> 01:09:52.880
Okay then.
那好吧。

1615
01:09:53.020 --> 01:09:54.040
And he leaves.
然后他离开了。

1616
01:09:54.520 --> 01:10:00.000
Dwight looks out the window as Kelly waits for Charles, sitting on the hood of his car sexily.
迪怀特看着窗外，而凯莉在等查尔斯，性感地坐在他汽车的引擎盖上。

1617
01:10:00.220 --> 01:10:01.240
Oh my gosh!
噢天哪！

1618
01:10:01.580 --> 01:10:05.180
As Charles approaches, we see Kelly is sitting on the wrong car.
当查尔斯走近时，我们发现凯莉坐错了车。

1619
01:10:05.720 --> 01:10:08.680
She runs over to Charles but doesn't get there in time.
她朝查尔斯跑去，但没赶上。

1620
01:10:08.900 --> 01:10:11.040
She bangs on the window as he drives off.
在他开车离开时，她用力拍打着车窗。

1621
01:10:11.300 --> 01:10:12.580
Charles talking head.
查尔斯单人访谈。

1622
01:10:13.120 --> 01:10:14.980
Never sleep with co-workers, man.
千万别和同事睡觉，老兄。

1623
01:10:14.980 --> 01:10:15.740
What?
什么？

1624
01:10:16.080 --> 01:10:17.120
Wait, what?
等等，什么？

1625
01:10:17.360 --> 01:10:19.020
That's what it ended with!
剧集就是以这个结尾的！

1626
01:10:19.640 --> 01:10:20.240
Wait.
等等。

1627
01:10:20.760 --> 01:10:21.720
Co-workers?
同事？

1628
01:10:22.360 --> 01:10:23.660
That's what it said.
剧本上就是这么写的。

1629
01:10:23.920 --> 01:10:25.760
Never sleep with co-workers, man.
千万别和同事睡觉，老兄。

1630
01:10:26.340 --> 01:10:26.840
Okay.
好吧。

1631
01:10:27.680 --> 01:10:29.180
What the heck?
搞什么鬼？

1632
01:10:29.660 --> 01:10:32.420
That was the ending to this episode.
这就是这一集的结局。

1633
01:10:32.660 --> 01:10:34.860
Angela walks up to him, says it was an honor.
安吉拉走到他身边，说这是荣幸。

1634
01:10:35.320 --> 01:10:38.060
Kelly tries to sit on his car before he leaves.
凯莉在他离开前试图坐上他的车。

1635
01:10:38.440 --> 01:10:38.740
Hmm.
嗯。

1636
01:10:39.220 --> 01:10:40.320
I don't know.
我不知道。

1637
01:10:40.820 --> 01:10:41.420
Wow.
哇。

1638
01:10:41.640 --> 01:10:42.240
I know!
就是说啊！

1639
01:10:42.640 --> 01:10:44.680
I was like, I have to share that.
我当时就想，我必须分享这个。

1640
01:10:45.220 --> 01:10:46.100
Okay, well, listen.
好吧，听着。

1641
01:10:46.260 --> 01:10:53.520
I'll have you know that in a very early draft, like one of the earliest outlines for this episode, there was another tag.
我得告诉你们，在一个非常早期的草稿里，也就是这集最早的大纲之一里，还有另一个尾声。

1642
01:10:53.900 --> 01:10:56.300
Now, this one didn't even make it into the shooting draft.
而且这个甚至都没能进入拍摄定稿。

1643
01:10:56.400 --> 01:10:57.980
Okay, because I don't know about this one.
好吧，因为我对这个一无所知。

1644
01:10:58.080 --> 01:10:59.080
Listen to this.
听听这个。

1645
01:10:59.180 --> 01:11:00.800
My lady, where did you find this?
小姐，你是从哪找到这个的？

1646
01:11:00.980 --> 01:11:02.040
Randy Cordray.
兰迪·科德雷。

1647
01:11:02.340 --> 01:11:02.720
Oh, Randy.
哦，兰迪。

1648
01:11:03.240 --> 01:11:04.520
Here's what it would have been.
原本的剧情会是这样的。

1649
01:11:04.900 --> 01:11:08.600
And I am so bummed that we did not get to do this.
我太遗憾我们没能拍成这一段了。

1650
01:11:08.600 --> 01:11:18.660
You were going to see Pam, Michael, and Ryan packing up Michael Scott Paper Company, and before they go, Michael is going to give them each a Scotty,
你们本来会看到帕姆、迈克尔和瑞安在收拾迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司，在他们离开前，迈克尔打算送他们每人一个小斯科蒂，

1651
01:11:18.860 --> 01:11:23.000
which is the Michael Scott Paper Company version of a Dundee.
这就是邓迪奖的迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司版。

1652
01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:24.940
Oh, with a little Scotty dog?
哦，带有小苏格兰梗犬吗？

1653
01:11:25.600 --> 01:11:27.220
No, no, because Michael Scott.
不，不，因为那是迈克尔·斯科特。

1654
01:11:27.680 --> 01:11:28.100
Oh.
哦。

1655
01:11:33.640 --> 01:11:38.280
I thought instead of the man with the briefcase, it was a little Scotty dog.
我还以为不是拿公文包的那个小人，而是一只小苏格兰梗犬呢。

1656
01:11:38.520 --> 01:11:38.800
No.
不是。

1657
01:11:38.880 --> 01:11:40.220
I got really excited.
我当时可激动了。

1658
01:11:40.220 --> 01:11:45.560
It didn't get far enough to know what the statue would be, but they were going to be called Scotty's.
虽然没进展到知道雕像具体会长什么样，但它们本来打算叫“斯科蒂奖”。

1659
01:11:45.560 --> 01:11:46.780
Instead of Dundee's.
而不是“邓迪奖”。

1660
01:11:46.780 --> 01:11:47.740
Instead of Dundee's.
而不是“邓迪奖”。

1661
01:11:47.960 --> 01:11:54.680
And Ryan was going to win one that said, great style, and Pam's said, boobs.
而且赖恩本来会赢得一个写着“极具风格”，而帕姆的写着“大胸”。

1662
01:11:55.740 --> 01:11:56.940
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

1663
01:11:57.300 --> 01:11:58.200
So good.
太棒了。

1664
01:11:58.700 --> 01:12:00.020
Pam got a Scotty.
帕姆拿到了一个斯科蒂奖。

1665
01:12:00.340 --> 01:12:08.300
Man, I have my Dundee's, both my whitest sneakers and my longest engagement, and I so wish I had a Scotty that said boobs.
天哪，我有我的邓迪奖，既有最白球鞋奖，也有最长订婚奖，我太希望能有一个写着“大胸”的斯科蒂奖了。

1666
01:12:08.300 --> 01:12:11.480
I have my Dundee's right next to my Emmy and my SAG Awards.
我的邓迪奖就摆在我的艾美奖和演员工会奖旁边。

1667
01:12:11.660 --> 01:12:13.320
I'm so jealous you have a real Emmy.
你居然有真正的艾美奖，我太嫉妒了。

1668
01:12:13.760 --> 01:12:14.440
I know.
我知道。

1669
01:12:15.160 --> 01:12:18.120
Angela won an Emmy for the webisodes.
安吉拉因为网络剧集赢过一个艾美奖。

1670
01:12:18.340 --> 01:12:19.160
The accountants.
《会计师》那一档。

1671
01:12:19.340 --> 01:12:21.860
Me and Brian and Oscar won an Emmy, you guys.
我和布莱恩还有奥斯卡赢过一个艾美奖，伙计们。

1672
01:12:22.220 --> 01:12:23.400
It was really amazing.
那真的很了不起。

1673
01:12:23.660 --> 01:12:29.920
But what sits right next to my Emmy that more people want to point out when they come to my house are my two Dundee's.
但是，摆在我艾美奖旁边、当别人来我家时最想指出来让我看的，其实是我的两个邓迪奖。

1674
01:12:30.340 --> 01:12:32.860
Titus asks, and she's kind of a bitch.
蒂塔斯问起，而且她有点刻薄。

1675
01:12:33.160 --> 01:12:34.240
I've said this before.
我以前就说过。

1676
01:12:34.420 --> 01:12:38.100
I am really bummed that I did not win an Emmy for Pam.
我真的很沮丧，我没能为帕姆赢得一个艾美奖。

1677
01:12:38.300 --> 01:12:39.400
For Pam.
为了帕姆。

1678
01:12:39.840 --> 01:12:42.140
I wanted our gal Pam to win that award.
我好想让我们家帕姆赢得那个奖。

1679
01:12:42.440 --> 01:12:44.720
I'll tell you what award Jenna wants to win.
我跟你说詹娜想赢得什么奖。

1680
01:12:44.860 --> 01:12:45.200
What?
什么？

1681
01:12:45.500 --> 01:12:46.580
A Tony Award.
托尼奖。

1682
01:12:47.400 --> 01:12:59.400
So my plan, after my kids are grown, I am going to retire in New York City, and I am going to work hard to get myself in a great Broadway show.
所以我的计划是，等我的孩子们长大了，我要去纽约市退休，然后我要努力争取参演一部百老汇大戏。

1683
01:12:59.400 --> 01:13:01.980
I'm going to give the performance of my life.
我要献出我一生中最精彩的表演。

1684
01:13:02.140 --> 01:13:06.400
I will vote for you even though I'm not a registered Tony voter.
我会为你投票，尽管我不是注册的托尼奖评委。

1685
01:13:06.560 --> 01:13:07.200
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1686
01:13:07.200 --> 01:13:08.860
And I want to win a Tony.
而且我想赢得一个托尼奖。

1687
01:13:09.580 --> 01:13:12.480
That's the award I want on my shelf more than any other award.
那是比起其他任何奖项，我更想摆在书架上的奖。

1688
01:13:12.740 --> 01:13:14.420
I want that for you so desperately.
我无比渴望你能得到它。

1689
01:13:14.460 --> 01:13:15.500
I hope it can happen.
我希望这能实现。

1690
01:13:15.880 --> 01:13:16.700
I want a Grammy.
我想要一个格莱美奖。

1691
01:13:17.280 --> 01:13:19.180
Ooh, you aren't a singer.
噢，你又不是歌手。

1692
01:13:19.480 --> 01:13:20.160
I know.
我知道。

1693
01:13:20.160 --> 01:13:21.640
Oh, I know.
哦，我懂。

1694
01:13:21.920 --> 01:13:23.040
I want a Grammy.
我想要一个格莱美奖。

1695
01:13:23.040 --> 01:13:29.240
Because, guys, Jenna and I recently found out that with our book, we'll be doing an audio book.
因为，伙计们，詹娜和我最近发现，对于我们的书，我们将要出一版有声书。

1696
01:13:29.440 --> 01:13:32.360
We're very excited about doing the audio book.
我们对录制有声书感到非常兴奋。

1697
01:13:32.480 --> 01:13:39.040
And we found out if you really, really crush it, you can get nominated for a Grammy for your audio book.
我们发现如果你真的、真的做得极其出色，你的有声书是可以获得格莱美奖提名的。

1698
01:13:39.280 --> 01:13:42.740
Amy Poehler got nominated for a Grammy for her audio book.
艾米·波勒就曾因她的有声书获得过格莱美奖提名。

1699
01:13:42.740 --> 01:13:43.520
Yes, please.
好极了。

1700
01:13:43.980 --> 01:13:44.700
That's right.
没错。

1701
01:13:45.140 --> 01:13:46.240
I want a Grammy.
我想要个格莱美奖。

1702
01:13:46.680 --> 01:13:47.140
All right.
行啊。

1703
01:13:47.260 --> 01:13:48.620
Let's get that effing Grammy.
我们要拿下那个该死的格莱美。

1704
01:13:48.820 --> 01:13:50.940
Let's get the Grammy and then get you your Tony.
我们要拿下格莱美，然后再帮你拿个托尼奖。

1705
01:13:51.200 --> 01:13:52.960
We're going to get those awards this year.
我们今年要把这些奖项都收入囊中。

1706
01:13:53.040 --> 01:13:58.020
You get an award and you guys get an award because you're badasses and you get an award and you get an award.
你有一个奖，你们也有一个奖，因为你们太牛了，你也有个奖，你也有个奖。

1707
01:13:58.200 --> 01:13:59.260
Awards all around.
到处都是奖。

1708
01:13:59.500 --> 01:14:00.160
Awards everywhere.
奖项无处不在。

1709
01:14:00.740 --> 01:14:01.820
This was a great episode.
这一集太棒了。

1710
01:14:02.220 --> 01:14:03.600
I'm going to make you a Scotty.
我要给你做一个苏格兰梗。

1711
01:14:03.800 --> 01:14:04.600
Oh, will you?
真的吗？

1712
01:14:04.700 --> 01:14:05.980
Is it going to be a Scotty dog?
会是一个苏格兰梗犬吗？

1713
01:14:06.220 --> 01:14:07.000
What's it going to be?
到底会是什么？

1714
01:14:07.040 --> 01:14:09.700
It will be my interpretation of what a Scotty would be.
这将是我对苏格兰梗的理解。

1715
01:14:09.820 --> 01:14:11.300
And I'm going to make it myself.
而且我要亲自做。

1716
01:14:11.360 --> 01:14:17.880
So get ready for a second grade skill set of art and crafting coming your way.
所以准备好迎接小学二年级水平的手工艺品吧。

1717
01:14:18.000 --> 01:14:18.980
I will treasure it.
我会珍藏它的。

1718
01:14:19.140 --> 01:14:20.620
I'm going to get out my glue gun.
我要把我的热熔胶枪拿出来。

1719
01:14:20.760 --> 01:14:21.460
I'm not kidding.
我没开玩笑。

1720
01:14:21.540 --> 01:14:22.880
I'm going to make this myself.
我要亲手做这个。

1721
01:14:23.120 --> 01:14:28.100
If we gave out awards for our business of office ladies, which is actually...
如果我们为我们的办公室女士业务颁奖，其实……

1722
01:14:28.100 --> 01:14:29.500
I know what it would be called!
我知道该叫什么名字了！

1723
01:14:29.500 --> 01:14:30.280
Rambleys?
闲聊杯？

1724
01:14:30.800 --> 01:14:32.200
Oh, I was going to say...
哦，我本想说……

1725
